comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T05:49:53.687Z","harness:codex","Reproduction evidence: pnpm smoke:npx failed twice because the hard-coded 120000 ms bound killed npx and npm-exec while resolving the local 4.7 MB/1423-file tarball. The identical primary npx command completed with version 2026.9.3 after about 155 seconds and bunx completed in 1.4 seconds. A first 300000 ms correction passed the primary and bare-package paths but still timed out the distinct pm-cli alias cache entry; exact alias latency measurement is continuing before final calibration."
  "2026-09-04T06:23:33.978Z","harness:codex","Final repository verification: pnpm quality:static passed the complete mandatory static gate; node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage passed 603 files and 8,350 tests at exact 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines; pnpm security:scan, pnpm audit, documentation links, and package-artifact checks passed. GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning alert inventories were empty. The timeout unit suite passed all 24 tests; the final packed npx/bunx workflow remains in progress under the new finite bound and will be recorded separately at terminal state."
  "2026-09-04T06:42:50.012Z","harness:codex","Terminal packed acceptance: pnpm smoke:npx passed real npx and bunx installs plus package catalog/install, calendar mutation/read, upgrade dry-run, CLI consumer, and SDK consumer workflows at version 2026.9.3 with 13 packages. Exact-tree coverage passed 8,351 tests at 100/100/100/100 and static quality passed."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T06:22:43.332Z","harness:codex","Packed npx smoke timeouts must accommodate cold local-tarball dependency reification, including the package-name alias path; on this host valid installs exceeded 300 seconds even though the installed CLI completed successfully."
